I have recovered a childlike appreciation for my favorite game.  My
8-year-old son started his first game of nethack today.  I knew he
would grow too easily frustrated if he kept dying over and over, so I
started him a neutral human wizard in explore mode.

He has been having the best time and I have SOOO enjoyed listening to
him play.  For instance...all of a sudden he just starts cracking up
and says "I'm stuck in a bear trap! Ha ha ha ha!"

"My dog picked up 17 rocks.  How cool!"  

"I'm gonna quaff from this fountain.  Oh man!  A water nymph stole my
lizard corpse.  I'm not gonna do that again!"  (smart kid!)

"Oh man!  My dog fell asleep.  Bummer."

I had told him that magic missile was one of the very best spellbooks
for a wizard to find...so he squeals and jumps up and down "I have the
magic missile spell!  WOW!!!!"

This has been so fun for me!  I'm curious to see how he likes sokoban.
 He used to have a sokoban game on the linux box and played it all the
time.  :)

